          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd122d6dc1889d50fab432e7bf7aaee3d34496e86896526cef80d6f922291a9e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e7868cec1094144b1da78c0322c1c7c",
      "statement": "The paired-fidelity monitor is observe-only by construction: it runs under `torch.inference_mode()`, never contributes to the loss, and never drives checkpoint selection — `val/psnr` / `val/ssim` are declared only so the registry's `validate_monitor` accepts them as validatable monitors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L1-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a18ef56a296f7054c2e16f65485deaf58032217aa270a95fc8eaa82b304e402:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L82-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:816898ab80a9ed1563b1a55d4e27cf24332025a7d1b47b8c599f43ed0152bf68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b628f80b1948499bbce88485b6a1a4ff",
      "statement": "`VaeStage` (`src/manifold/metrics/vae_stage.py`) is the single VAE-only stage/restore implementation — it snapshots the VAE's CPU state, moves it to the device for a decode, and restores it to CPU even if `__enter__` fails partway — and `VramStage` (`src/manifold/metrics/fid/vram.py`) composes it, adding only the FID-specific feature-net build, so the paired-fidelity decode and FID cannot drift on the VRAM path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/fid/vram.py#L66-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ce3987d14795d0c462c5e55457708ca4a87366c8dd4733abf228339813c2367:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/vae_stage.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:cced06259497b2cb6857a30ad765865d1ccc878ab3e9a3c48de60671ef305563"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_069f5608fda548d8a10c0fe2a4973df0",
      "statement": "`PairedFidelitySpec` exposes the monitor's knobs (`subset_size`, `every_n_epochs`, `num_inference_steps`, `seed`) as dataclass fields validated by the callback registry, and the rollout step count is recipe-primary: `build` reads `num_inference_steps` from `CallbackContext.inference_recipe`, which the supervised shell fills from the existing `controlnet.num_inference_steps` config knob.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/paired_fidelity.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:09c5b8bb0451cd41f6c98d678177eb1d52639198fcd4bd89a0a29b6af1339273"
        },
        {
