          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b01bd7df459543ad33d9a286fbfaa54b25260b64d2e6a5e120cf431077dec97b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53b9c5756c8544ce8f4843770f00be2f",
      "statement": "The paired-fidelity monitor resolves its fixed validation subset lazily at the first gated epoch (`getattr(datamodule, \"val_latent_ds\", datamodule)`), so the cold path's post-`setup()` replacement of the warmed validation dataset is honored rather than captured at build time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/data/datamodule.py#L40-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16d609e42beb8162286062a63720504274cb54a7a4d90354334153a74aaa2586:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L125-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3175cd9f3cec4eb18fe33df9a6911bba48dd61d1cccc699a006b8f023224ee8b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e4b5ce61e0a4e3f9b778771eba0a4aa",
      "statement": "Under DDP the paired-fidelity monitor is redundant evaluation: every rank scores the same fixed subset under the same seeded noise on DDP-synchronized weights, so the only cross-rank interaction is Lightning's torchmetrics sync — no FID-style sharding or error-rendezvous machinery is needed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L22-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53e5296f948ef16052ab4a8dbcd5b65c117dc575d3f849d542bd7308aaf1d387:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_paired_fidelity_ddp.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:cc8f0743bf83fa5a93ef7607cf485eb72f8c8a5454d7e89f933ac62f133817a7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ed74949d8b6a46fdb1959271a4820768",
      "statement": "`TrainingSpine.run`'s merge order is the single source of truth for the callback set: default names → per-name knob overrides → a name-list replacement from the CLI `--callbacks` flag or the YAML `callbacks:` list, with `forbidden_callbacks` / `forbidden_monitors` enforced after the merge so no override can re-enable a forbidden callback or monitor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/config/loader.py#L155-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:236cc0aaeca209a4be379584db38dbf4585067a49256aad247c1b00baf3088b2:"
